            <ArticleTitle>Two cases of spontaneous middle cerebral arterial dissection causing ischemic stroke.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>162-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous middle cerebral arterial dissection (MCAD) is a rare cause of ischemic stroke. We report two cases of isolated spontaneous MCAD causing ischemic stroke. MCAD should be considered when a young patient has a middle cerebral artery territory infarct with stenosis at the origin of the middle cerebral artery. We discuss noninvasive radiological techniques for the diagnosis of MCAD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
